# CODEOWNERS — default reviewers per path.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the listed owners when a pull request touches a
# matching path. This names an account rather than a team on purpose: the
# `@trustedoss/maintainers` team the previous rules pointed at was never
# created, and GitHub silently assigns no reviewer for an owner that does not
# exist, so every rule here was inert.
#
# One person owns every path today, so there is one rule. Listing each
# directory separately would imply a split in review responsibility that does
# not exist. The per-path rules, and a team in place of the account, come back
# with the second maintainer (see MAINTAINERS.md and GOVERNANCE.md).

